and it certainly has been a very trying  time for our educators not just the last  year and some of the things that are  going on in the school district right  now but the past two years during the  pandemic so this week  simply a week to say thank you for all  you do absolutely a big thank you to all  of our educators bianca holman joining  us live this morning with how you can  recognize the educators in your child's  life bianca good morning  hey good morning so our teachers are  juggling a lot right now from school  violence to teacher shortage but this is  the time in the week to take a step back  and say thank you for all that they do  and share our gratitude and share our  appreciation for investing in our kids  now the national pta they created  teacher appreciation week this year it's  important to show your appreciation for  your educators even at the middle and  high school level not just for our  elementary school educators  we spoke with rebecca garcia of nevada  pta and she says it's so important to  make sure teachers know we value their  work that they do the effort that they  put into preparing our children for the  future  i think teacher appreciation week is a  good time to stop  and make sure that as a parent as a  family member you're acknowledging the  hard work that teachers do you're  saying thank you and encouraging your  kids to do the same  garcia also says it's not all about the  gifts flowers gift cards and things like  that but a handwritten note that can  make a huge impact individual schools of  course are doing their own thing and  celebrating in their own ways but there  are tons of stores like barnes and noble  and j crew national stores that have  discounts for educators this week up  next in the next half hour we're going  to talk with an educator about his  experience and what this week means to  him and also some things here locally  that are in benefit of and celebrating  our educators that are across the valley  bianca holman live local now
 

